found = search_by_id(students, id)
if found: print('Found student with ID {}: {}, GPA: {}'.format(found.id, found.name, found.gpa)) 
else: print('Student not found')
```

Please note that this is a simple example and doesn't account for any edge cases or error handling you might want in a real-world application. Also, the `search_by_name` function will return all students with matching names, if there are multiple students with the same name. In a more realistic scenario, you might want to modify this function to return only one result or raise an exception if multiple results are found.
